# Template for /home/ledio/egyptology.env (chmod 600; never commit the real one).
# Read by systemd as an EnvironmentFile and by scripts/egyptology-deploy.sh with a small
# parser, so the format is strict: KEY=value, one per line, no quotes, no spaces around
# the "=", no `export`. A value may contain spaces or $; it is taken literally.

# Passphrase that unlocks annotation saving and the private rows. Leave empty to disable.
REVIEWER_KEY=

# ntfy.sh topic for failure notifications (see egyptology-notify@.service). A long
# random string: anyone who knows it can read and post to it. Empty on purpose: a
# placeholder would be a public topic anyone can guess, so fill in your own (for example
# `openssl rand -hex 16`); until then the notify unit fails visibly in the journal.
NTFY_TOPIC=

# healthchecks.io ping URL for the nightly backup (pinged on success, /fail on failure).
# HEALTHCHECK_URL=https://hc-ping.com/CHANGE_ME

# Where the SQLite database lives. Set this ONLY after the file has been moved there
# (DEPLOYMENT.md, "Moving the database out of the clone"), otherwise the app creates and
# seeds a fresh, empty database at the new path.
# DATABASE_URL=sqlite:////home/ledio/egyptology-data/egyptology.db

# Off-site prune from the backup script: set 0 once the B2 key cannot delete files.
# OFFSITE_PRUNE=0
